  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title><para>Consider the inequality \( -\frac12 x + 6 &lt; 4x−3 \). Let’s look at another way to find its solutions.</para>
<!--BEGIN ADD DESMOS INTERATIVE-->
<!--START QUESTION #1 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Graph \(y=-\frac12 x + 6 \)and \(y=4x−3\) on the same coordinate plane using the Desmos tool below. </item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <!--question moved outside of interactino due to DESMOS -->
  <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <!--REPLACE IMAGE BELOW WITH CORRECT IMAGE-->
  <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3de7e6fae22f182297a1b8cbf6f6733973a8005f"/></media></figure></solution></exercise>
</example><!--END ADD DESMOS INTERATIVE-->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<para>Use your graphs to answer the following questions:</para>
<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Find the values of \( -\frac {1}{2}x+6 \) and \( 4x-3 \) when \( x \) is 1.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>When \( x \) is 1, find the value of \( - \frac{1}{2} x+6 \) is \( 5 \frac{1}{2} \), and the value of \( 4x-3 \) is 1.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What value of \( x \) makes \( -\frac {1}{2}x+6 \) and \( 4x-3 \) equal?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>When \( x \) is equal to 2, the value of \( - \frac{1}{2} x+6 \) is equal to that of \( 4x-2 \).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>For what values of \( x \) is \( - \frac12 x + 6 \) less than \( 4x−3 \)?
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>When \( x \) is greater than 2, the value of \( - \frac{1}{2} x+6 \) is less than that of \(4x-3\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!--Q#5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>For what values of \( x \) is \( - \frac12 x + 6 \) greater than \( 4x−3 \)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>When \( x \) is less than 2, the value of \( - \frac{1}{2} x+6 \) is greater than that of \( 4x-3 \).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the solution to the inequality \( - \frac12 x+ 6 &lt; 4x−3 \)? Be prepared to explain how you know.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: \( x &gt;2 \)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
